  "notes": "\"The reason the abrasive art-rap wing sounds like post-punk rather than Atlanta.\" The research's central claim is harmonic and it is unusually blunt: the sources run from krautrock and library electronics (Guru Guru, Delia Derbyshire, Nick Mason) to Chinese pop and noise (Cut Hands), \"the 'progression' is whatever the loop implies, usually a single unstable minor or **whole-tone** cell\", and \"the harmonic instability is the point\". So `whole_tone` carries real weight in the scale pool alongside `chromatic`, `chordToneBias` drops to 0.3 — the lowest in this batch — and `halfStepDissonance` rises to 0.45. This is not a trap grid: the documented default is 85–105 straight with a 2-and-4 backbeat plus 120–130 four-on-the-floor techno-facing sections, so `halfTime` is off, `snare.placement` is `backbeat_24`, the kick reaches five hits a bar for the four-on-the-floor cuts, and there is 8th-note swing at 0.56. \"Sampled live drums ... deliberately dry and forward\" is authored as the *loudest* tiers here (accents 110–127, mains 90–106) at a low `quantizeStrength` of 0.7 and `velocityVar` 0.24, because the feel comes from the sampled source rather than programming. \"Frequently no 808 — low end is the filtered sample or a distorted analogue-style synth bass\" is `bassline.rhythm` `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.5 across a 30–49 sample-bass register with `bass808.sustain` `staccato`. \"Loop-point glitches left in\" is `emptyBarBias` 0.12 over 2- and 4-bar cells, and `timbreHint` is `spacey_keys` for the library-electronics palette. ⚠ `medium` matches the research: his role, sample sources, studios and the record's sonic character are documented, but no reachable interview on his own technique exists, so the INFERRED parameters — marked `[LOW-CONF]` in the paragraph — are the drum numbers and the tempo range. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.2 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.2 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub. ⚠ The chord voicing moved up to [50, 90] so the bass stays under the harmony — it started at 40 against a bass reaching 49, an overlap of 10. The span is preserved; a voicing that low was competing with the bass rather than sitting over it.",
